{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/490960-nosferatu-clan-curse-ideas","id":490960,"title":"Nosferatu: Clan Curse Ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-24T14:54:14-07:00","id":490960,"title":"Nosferatu: Clan Curse Ideas","content":"Back in Vt:M, the Nos were all universally hideous and deformed, so they just failed at any interaction requiring physical appearance.<br /> <br /> I've actually been really happy with the way the new Nosferatu clan weakness has manifested. I like the idea that you don't have to be terrifyingly ugly as a Haunt, but that something else is just . . . wrong, about you. I love that with a high Presence, or even Majesty or Dominate, you can surmount some of your Curse . . . but if you fail, you fail hard no matter what.<br /> <br /> To that end, I'm curious what other people have come up with to describe their character's bane and the way it manifests (if at all; obviously even if you cover up whatever's physically not right, there's still that aura of strangeness that still unsettles mortals, but that's beside the point).<br /> <br /> I'll offer a few starters:<br /> <br /> <b>Elena Kerensky:</b> A woman in her thirties with a patrician air to her, she's fairly average-to-attractive, but she's a touch pale\u2014almost with a faint blue-green undertone in the right light. This, along with the slight dampness to her skin and the smell of salt and water that constantly clings to her, almost gives her the air of a drowning victim.<br /> <br /> <b>Violet Madrone:</b> This girl is incredibly beautiful. She's perfect. Too perfect. In fact, she's one-hundred-percent symmetrical, head to toe. From the arc of her hairline to the porcelain skin of her brow to her sapphire-toned eyes to her golden-ratio perfect nose to her full cupid's-bow lips to her gently pointed cheekbones and chin, either side of her face is a perfectly symmetrical match to the other. She's like a living doll, a creature that just climbed out of the depths of the Uncanny Valley.<br /> <br /> <b>Phillip Karlsson</b>: A tall, slender, athletic man, with a receding hairline and slightly elongated, rodentine features. He's calm, composed, unobtrusive. In fact, unless he actively speaks or makes effort to engage with you, he almost seems to immediately fade into the background. Almost, but not quite. His presence kind of wavers right on that border, just like that feeling you get when you twitch awake, not having noticed you were about to fall asleep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T15:10:34-07:00","id":490988,"title":"","content":"<b>BBQ Girl</b>: A wide-faced, friendly young woman, with mildly frazzled hair and a sturdy neck. Despite her job as a grill cook and her namelessness and her minimum-wage aura, she's got a confident face. A stern face. A stiff face, in fact. It's like she's done something surgical to freeze her expression, only there's something so... painted on about her freckles, her eyes, her lips, as if they're illustrations on an external paper stretched over a hard rim. Occasionally, her skin shifts alignment on her head, so she looks like her face is slightly detached from the axis of symmetry. There's a patch of skin missing on her brow, under her hairline; underneath is warm, slightly rusty metal, two visible rivets and a hole that seems to open into a dark red nothing. She <i>says</i> it's from surgery. She always smells like grease and fat and blood, for more than one reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5757-calvaryketer","name":"CalvaryKeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5757_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T17:56:04-07:00","id":491101,"title":"","content":"<b>Slink:</b> She's damn graceful. When she walks it's like tall grass blowing in the breeze. Flowing. Effortless. When she dances... man. Have you ever seen one of those gymnasts that twirl those long ribbons? It's like that. Hypnotic. But then, you start to notice stuff. Just something little at first, at a glance, that didn't look right. Keep watching long enough and you'll see her scratch an itch on the back of her hand, with the fingers on <i>that</i> hand. She covers it well most of the time, but when she's scared, or excited, or pissed, I've seen her turn her head all the way around like a damn owl. None of her joints ever hit the backstop, ya know? Every single one of them folds as far back as it does forward. I saw her frenzy once, she chased a guy down and when she was running, she just... she just like <i>rolled </i>over everything in the alley until she wrapped him up. I try not to think about it anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T18:22:53-07:00","id":491136,"title":"","content":"<b>Mr. Grove</b> is behind you. No, that can't be right. He's over there, sitting and talking with that other guy. But you could swear <i>someone</i> is right behind you, too close for comfort, every time Mr. Grove talks to you, or just looks your way. Or when you think about him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T18:32:03-07:00","id":491139,"title":"","content":"John Waters.<br /> <br /> These are really great, you guys! Anyone got any cool ideas on how to characterize a Nosferatu that inspires a hateful reaction in the people through their curse?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T18:43:42-07:00","id":491142,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I'm not sure if it's his nickname or what. Maybe some Estate bigwig started calling him that but it stuck. Whatever it is, you gotta know a few things going in about Johnny Grunt. He's smart, yeah? He's connected. He's got fingers in the cacophony that I don't know what. He's got the pull to get you the best rigs and loadouts you could hope for. But here's the thing - he's fuckin' gross. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The Almoner told me something went wrong with Grunt's throat. For most of us, the vitae keeps our vocal cords nice and slick, but for him - dry as shit. If he's not coughing, he's wheezing. Barely gets a few words out without his voice cracking and sputtering. He found a way around it, but I'm not sure it's better. He eats things. Sloppy fuckin' things. Runny cheese, weird sauces, french toasts and syrup - he snarfs it down right there in front of you. I'm honestly not sure which is better, watching him cough up a lung trying to give you the information you paid for, or watching him shovel that shit down his gullet so he gets out a few paragraphs without stopping.</span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/490960-nosferatu-clan-curse-ideas?p=491139#post491139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are really great, you guys! Anyone got any cool ideas on how to characterize a Nosferatu that inspires a hateful reaction in the people through their curse?</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't played it yet, but have considered playing a 'protected minority' Nos type. In other words, what if the curse manifested in making people jump immediately to antisemitism, or sexism, or homophobia, or racism - even if they normally weren't the type to do so. Think the Alec Baldwin F-Bomb scandal. People who normally seem progressive, but who regress during anger or stress to hate speech. For the particular Haunt, people jump to that extreme when around them. Maybe they feel bad later, maybe they don't - but the Haunt themselves sort of brings it on","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","user":"Holy","date":". 04-24-2015, 10:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T19:08:42-07:00","id":491170,"title":"","content":"<b>Bacon Strips:</b> A physically in shape man who appears to be in his early 30's. The muscles on him indicates someone who routinely works out either as a hobby or because his job requires an above average physique to perform. He is clean shaven and bald, with a friendly disposition and a square jawline. Unfortunately he suffers a terrible skin condition from which he gets his name; across his body are streaks of exposed muscle tissue from where his skin has been peeled or flayed off his body. The pattern resembles tiger stripes along his head, arms, legs and back. It's easy enough to hide the rest of his wounds, but the head is the more difficult feature, generally requiring him to wear shadowy hoods or a mask of some sort when in public,<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Grandpa Harold:</b> To the casual observer, Grandpa (who he insists on being referred to by) appears to be an ordinary man in the state of advanced age. Like, really advanced age... like, why isn't this guy hooked up to a life support machine yet? Grandpa's body is withered to the point of near mummification. His hair is ghost white and is so thin it seems like cobwebs floating about his head. His face is sunken and his eyes seem hollow as they never open wider than a half squint when he's feeling a surge of emotion. When in public, Grandpa Harold is confined to his wheel chair, holding a walking cane over his lap, and with a rather attractive nurse pushing him where he plans to go. Grandpa Harold loves to tell stories of his youth both as a human and as a vampire, and many kindred respect him for the experience he has to offer. Those who lack proper respect, however, receive a swift cane across their backsides!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Katie, the Slob: </b>One of the Nosferatu who was lucky enough to retain her mortal visage, Katie is easily able to disguise herself as a human. Unfortunately it takes more than physical appearance to make her popular around the community, and Katie is almost universally despised because of her crude, vulgar and downright unseemly mannerisms. More than once she has been caught picking her nose in public and then wiping it on her clothes or even the environment around her. Sometimes on other people if she thinks she isn't being watched! She belches loudly and without covering her mouth and swears like a sailor during conversation. She appears to have no shame when discussing sensitive matters or secrets and no matter how high in the status quo she is associating with, she speaks with them in a casual, flippant manner. She wears the same clothing for days at a time, accumulating various stains throughout the weeks and appears to do her laundry once every 6 months. She forgoes bathing for 3 or 4 days on average, and her hair is left wild and unkempt. Katie, the Slob offends everyone within sight and sound of her location, and unless they have business with her, most try to avoid getting close enough to strike up a conversation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-25-2015, 12:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T22:01:09-07:00","id":491342,"title":"","content":"These are all really great ideas. I'd love to see what else everyone comes up with <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/490960-nosferatu-clan-curse-ideas?p=491139#post491139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">John Waters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, nicely done. I literally burst out laughing helplessly the moment I read this. +1 V-rep. :P<br /> <br /> Meanwhile . . .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/490960-nosferatu-clan-curse-ideas?p=491142#post491142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't played it yet, but have considered playing a 'protected minority' Nos type. In other words, what if the curse manifested in making people jump immediately to antisemitism, or sexism, or homophobia, or racism - even if they normally weren't the type to do so. Think the Alec Baldwin F-Bomb scandal. People who normally seem progressive, but who regress during anger or stress to hate speech. For the particular Haunt, people jump to that extreme when around them. Maybe they feel bad later, maybe they don't - but the Haunt themselves sort of brings it on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Holy, that's . . . actually an <u>awesome</u> idea. I was trying to come up with ways that the Lonely Curse would impact others, and this is an amazing thought.<br /> <br /> (In the last game I was running, I definitely played up The Contaminant Worm aspect of the Kindred condition; for example, a well-to-do high-rise apartment building that ended up inhabited and owned by Violet Madrone became this lovely, secure, spotlessly clean, but sterile, cold place that looked like it was inhabited by the likes of Patrick Bateman from <i>American Psycho</i> and Zeke Hawkins from <i>Sliver</i>. The elevator hummed smoothly and a little <i>too</i> quietly, the shadows thrown by fluorescent hall lights\u2014which buzzed just the tiniest bit\u2014were just a shade <i>too </i>sharp, and as for the security cameras . . . anyway, the non-mechanical aspects are a big part of storytelling for me.)<br /> <br /> Holy's idea is a really impressive expression of both of Curse and Contamination. It's likely no one could ever put it together in concrete words, but they'd still be a little off-put by that character's presence, although not necessarily consciously, even if the character was otherwise totally normal. (To bastardize the line from <i>Fight Club, </i>after Tyler splices a single frame of porn into a family movie: &quot;They don't know that they saw it, but they did.&quot;)<br /> <br /> Hate and bad arguments would just seem to follow him, even if he's the nicest guy in the room. This actually stands out to me even more because of that particular psychological phenomenon everyone has, where part of your mind can sometimes just come up with the most horrible thoughts, even if you aren't necessarily racist, sexist, ableist, ageist, or any other -ist . . .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":583,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","user":"Zsander","date":". 04-25-2015, 01:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T02:12:57-07:00","id":491481,"title":"","content":"That Haunt who's always in your personal space. Not *just* your personal space. A *foot* too far into your personal space. Doesn't matter what you tell him, doesn't matter how hard he tries. He's. Always. There. Right beside...you.<br /> <br /> The Haunt who smiles when she should be crying. Scowls when she should be laughing. Every emotion on her face comes out in a twisted parody of the opposite emotion. The only time you ever know where she stands is when she feels nothing at all.<br /> <br /> He seems perfectly normal. Except when he's in your peripheral vision. Then you see the Haunt is staring at you. Staring right into your skull.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T03:38:07-07:00","id":491523,"title":"","content":"Her eyes don't move. Why don't they move? Seriously, when was the last time you saw her eyes do <i>anything</i> but stare directly forward, blinking occasionally? Talk about your thousand-mile stare...<br /> <br /> You know, Papa's a really nice guy. It's just that... with that thick black soot caked on his face <i>all the time</i>, it looks like he's wearing blackface. And that's just not cool. Not cool at all. Then there's the fact that he calls women &quot;Dave&quot;. Just... what?<br /> <br /> The Haunt who seems to have forgotten that you can see things below your waist; oh, sure, he navigates just fine, but I wish he'd put on pants.<br /> <br /> Ever since Sandra was Embraced, she developed the thickest European accent; she spontaneously seems to swap between accents from England and Greece and everywhere in-between. Sometimes, she changes accent in the middle of a sentence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T05:59:52-07:00","id":491580,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Stumps Mcgee:</b> Something went wrong with his embrace. No, he didn't become a larvae or some other abomination, it's just a unique condition for which nobody seems to have an explanation for. Mcgee's body seems to have a defective preservation ability. Every night he wakes up, a random body part has rotted and festered, sometimes even falling off depending on where it is located. The rot apparently lasts for 24 hours because the following night, it has been reconstituted, only for a different piece to take on the affliction!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Cupcake:</b> She's the sweetest girl in the city, and that's the problem. The girl who is affectionately referred to as &quot;Cupcake&quot; is just too energetic, too bubbly, too friendly, and too aggravating for other people's taste. Staying in the same room as her for longer than 5 minutes quickly becomes grating on one's nerves. She often wears pink and bedazzles her clothes with fake gems and glitter. She even still wears her hair in pigtails and has key chains with her favorite characters attached to them. Her Haven is littered with stuffed animals, silly wallpaper and kitten posters, and she will not hesitate to sing the jingles of infomercials and children's broadcasts when they air on TV. In Cupcake's attempt to be cute and friendly, she comes off as childish and obnoxious!</span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-26-2015, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T06:45:53-07:00","id":492556,"title":"","content":"<b>Maximilian Dean: </b>He's always felt like an outsider because his curse has manifested in one of the most literal ways possible. Maximilian is drawn to ideas, organizations, and occupations that separate him from society by their very natures. As a member of the Ordo Dracul, he is a natural scientist. His curse is his refusal to let go of provably wrong theories, and indeed, his willingness to adopt the most bizarre ideas and methodologies. He has been, at various times in his existence, a phrenologist, a lobotomist, a member of the Ordo Templi Orientis. All occupations completely out of sync with modern science. His current Mask is the behind-the-scenes leader of a Church of Scientology. These attributes would be bad enough, except he is also the primogen for the Nosferatu in his city. All of the other Kindred in the city must eventually deal with him and he is about to make his move to replace the current prince. For those in the know, they can only imagine the chaos he'll plunge the city into should he ever achieve that goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1257-kerensky","name":"Kerensky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T07:51:13-07:00","id":492583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kerensky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/490960-nosferatu-clan-curse-ideas?p=492556#post492556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Maximilian Dean: </b>He's always felt like an outsider because his curse has manifested in one of the most literal ways possible. Maximilian is drawn to ideas, organizations, and occupations that separate him from society by their very natures. As a member of the Ordo Dracul, he is a natural scientist. His curse is his refusal to let go of provably wrong theories, and indeed, his willingness to adopt the most bizarre ideas and methodologies. He has been, at various times in his existence, a phrenologist, a lobotomist, a member of the Ordo Templi Orientis. All occupations completely out of sync with modern science. His current Mask is the behind-the-scenes leader of a Church of Scientology. These attributes would be bad enough, except he is also the primogen for the Nosferatu in his city. All of the other Kindred in the city must eventually deal with him and he is about to make his move to replace the current prince. For those in the know, they can only imagine the chaos he'll plunge the city into should he ever achieve that goal.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> while a great character concept, I just fail to see this as a proper Nosferatu clan bane manifestation... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T09:21:11-07:00","id":492655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/490960-nosferatu-clan-curse-ideas?p=492583#post492583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> while a great character concept, I just fail to see this as a proper Nosferatu clan bane manifestation... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that there's some &quot;mechanical&quot; flaw on it... I think it only needs a small adjustment to grant that the curse manifests itself both at long (as it's currently presented) and short run.<br /> <br /> Maybe... something like an aura of &quot;intelectual chalenge&quot; mixed with a &quot;blas\u00e8&quot; attitude around the character.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/646-mabafu","name":"mabafu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T09:39:54-07:00","id":492661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mabafu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/490960-nosferatu-clan-curse-ideas?p=492655#post492655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree that there's some &quot;mechanical&quot; flaw on it... I think it only needs a small adjustment to grant that the curse manifests itself both at long (as it's currently presented) and short run.<br /> <br /> Maybe... something like an aura of &quot;intelectual chalenge&quot; mixed with a &quot;blas\u00e8&quot; attitude around the character.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, but in that case the &quot; aura of &quot;intelectual chalenge&quot; mixed with a &quot;blas\u00e8&quot; attitude around the character.&quot; part is gonna be the bane, with the rest of it being characters fluff and background. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T12:13:54-07:00","id":492788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/490960-nosferatu-clan-curse-ideas?p=492661#post492661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, but in that case the &quot; aura of &quot;intelectual chalenge&quot; mixed with a &quot;blas\u00e8&quot; attitude around the character.&quot; part is gonna be the bane, with the rest of it being characters fluff and background. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually... in this case, being the curse concept as orignal as it was presented by Kerensky, I honestly believe that the correct is to consider plain mechanics as the &quot;fluff&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The idea of an incongruent scientist, a despised theoretician, and a lone researcher mixed altogheter is simply too cool!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/646-mabafu","name":"mabafu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T12:39:41-07:00","id":492802,"title":"","content":"Good stuff here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T23:54:56-07:00","id":493341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mabafu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/490960-nosferatu-clan-curse-ideas?p=492788#post492788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually... in this case, being the curse concept as orignal as it was presented by Kerensky, I honestly believe that the correct is to consider plain mechanics as the &quot;fluff&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The idea of an incongruent scientist, a despised theoretician, and a lone researcher mixed altogheter is simply too cool!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, the idea is super awesome. As I said before. However, making this his &quot;curse&quot; seems backwards to me. He might have been pushed to such lifestyle by the curse, but... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T06:47:12-07:00","id":493547,"title":"","content":"Wow. Sparked some conversations with that one. I've been thinking about the mechanical aspect though and I think a modified version of the Delusional condition would work best. His delusions apply to the theories and science as stated before, and when one either wears too thin or his interest is pulled by new ideas, the delusion switches to the flavor of the decade. Since the condition doesn't actually impose any mechanical problems (save the willpower expenditure), the manifestation... The &quot;fluff&quot; caused by the condition would translate into the clan bane penalties. People are so disturbed by his beliefs and occupations, that he takes the social penalty. And really, who would trust or believe such a loon, which gives us the Presence and Manipulation failures.<br /> <br /> How's that sound?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1257-kerensky","name":"Kerensky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T06:49:30-07:00","id":493550,"title":"","content":"So basically he comes across as a disturbing crackpot, and people tend to reject whatever he says?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T06:53:07-07:00","id":493554,"title":"","content":"Pretty much. First time I had my players meet him, he was offering them free personality tests and trying to get them to sign up for clearing sessions (Scientology babble.) Next time he was practicing phrenology on one of his ghouls, still struggling with letting that occupation go. It produced so many valid results, you know?<br /> <br /> He's tried to manipulate them using quack science (and veiled threats through the practice of that science) since night one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1257-kerensky","name":"Kerensky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T06:55:14-07:00","id":493556,"title":"","content":"Becoming isolated because people don't ever put stock in anything you say works perfectly for the Nosferatu bane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T07:18:50-07:00","id":493573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kerensky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/490960-nosferatu-clan-curse-ideas?p=493547#post493547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow. Sparked some conversations with that one. I've been thinking about the mechanical aspect though and I think a modified version of the Delusional condition would work best. His delusions apply to the theories and science as stated before, and when one either wears too thin or his interest is pulled by new ideas, the delusion switches to the flavor of the decade. Since the condition doesn't actually impose any mechanical problems (save the willpower expenditure), the manifestation... The &quot;fluff&quot; caused by the condition would translate into the clan bane penalties. People are so disturbed by his beliefs and occupations, that he takes the social penalty. And really, who would trust or believe such a loon, which gives us the Presence and Manipulation failures.<br /> <br /> How's that sound?</div> </div> </div> </div>My only concern about that kind of approach is that the curse would only manifests after a considerable interation with the character. Being it a NPC, I don't see any problem, but PCs could abuse it (you know.. they could <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kerensky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/490960-nosferatu-clan-curse-ideas?p=493554#post493554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much. First time I had my players meet him, he was offering them free personality tests and trying to get them to sign up for clearing sessions (Scientology babble.) Next time he was practicing phrenology on one of his ghouls, still struggling with letting that occupation go. It produced so many valid results, you know?<br /> <br /> He's tried to manipulate them using quack science (and veiled threats through the practice of that science) since night one.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one the best revamps I've ever seen of the REAL old Malkavian concept... I think Onyx Path should consider Nosfies being the parent clan from now... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/646-mabafu","name":"mabafu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T07:21:56-07:00","id":493576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mabafu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/490960-nosferatu-clan-curse-ideas?p=493573#post493573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My only concern about that kind of approach is that the curse would only manifests after a considerable interation with the character. Being it a NPC, I don't see any problem, but PCs could abuse it (you know.. they could <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it ends up working like Disquiet from Promethean. Nosferatu and Prometheans share some of that design space, of course, but it's better that the mechanics work differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T09:08:10-07:00","id":493668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zsander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/490960-nosferatu-clan-curse-ideas?p=491342#post491342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hate and bad arguments would just seem to follow him, even if he's the nicest guy in the room. This actually stands out to me even more because of that particular psychological phenomenon everyone has, where part of your mind can sometimes just come up with the most horrible thoughts, even if you aren't necessarily racist, sexist, ableist, ageist, or any other -ist . . .</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. And even if it's not a direct confrontation, hearing people around the Haunt making barely-whispered <i>anything-ist</i> comments, or hateful and unapproving glares at 'his kind' - whatever that is - would just make anything social awkward. <br /> <br /> In similar real-like 'awkward but unfair' effects is something I call the 'eternal victim.' I've known a couple people who just consistently have terrible things happen to them over and over. At first you are sympathetic, then you start thinking maybe they are just playing things up for sympathy and you distance yourself, but then you realize that they aren't making stuff up, but you really can't get yourself to be sympathetic anymore, and just sort of avoid interacting with them on a personal level. Like some sort of victim fatigue. <br /> <br /> It would be an easy spin to make it more about bad luck as opposed to victimization, too. Things break, drinks spill, traffic lights are always red. It never seems like the Haunt's 'fault' - but people interacting with them are just constantly frustrated by the (non-mechanical) mishaps and annoyances that surround the Nos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T12:41:29-07:00","id":493865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/490960-nosferatu-clan-curse-ideas?p=493668#post493668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be an easy spin to make it more about bad luck as opposed to victimization, too. Things break, drinks spill, traffic lights are always red. It never seems like the Haunt's 'fault' - but people interacting with them are just constantly frustrated by the (non-mechanical) mishaps and annoyances that surround the Nos.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sort of thing is why I think it's great that it's called The Lonely Curse (as opposed to the Spooky Curse or the Hideous Curse or whatnot). Whatever it is about the individual is so unsettling, either subtly or blatantly, that people would simply . . . rather not get near it. You wouldn't want it to rub off on you, now would you?<br /> <br /> These are all some neat ideas I've seen thus far by people, including Kerensky's\u2014the character just sounds like they cannot <i>shut up</i> about their outdated pseudoscience; not just as an obsession, but a compulsion. If you wanted to apply that sort of manifestation of the curse to a social interaction, say, hunting, think of Xavier in X-Men: First Class, where every time he hits on a girl, he starts up about some beautiful mutation or other that they have (hair, eyes, etc) . . . then take it a few steps further than that.<br /> <br /> (As an aside, re: the idea of Malkavia that someone else mentioned, I think even the Ventrue clanbook does say that Malkavia can possibly affect any Kindred . . .)<br /> <br /> <b>Another random curse idea:</b> Every time people spend a little while around her, they swear that they can hear something after awhile. It's like that ringing in your ears you get when it's too quiet, or you've been somewhere too loud. Could it . . . nah, it's probably nothing. It'll go away. But I thought I heard this . . . this <i>noise</i> . . .<br /> <br /> (As anyone with tinnitus can attest, its effects on the psyche can range from mildly distracting to suicidally maddening. Would tie in well with Nightmare, too).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":583,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","user":"Zsander","date":". 04-27-2015, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}